


FILE(1)             UNIX Programmer's Manual		  FILE(1)



NNAAMMEE
     file - determine file type

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ffiillee [ -ff name ]
     ffiillee file1 ... filen

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     _F_i_l_e performs a series of tests on each argument in an
     attempt to classify it.  If an argument appears to be ASCII,
     _f_i_l_e examines the first 512 bytes and tries to guess its
     language.

     If -f is used, _f_i_l_e reads its argument list from the file
     _n_a_m_e.

BBUUGGSS
     It often makes mistakes.  In particular it often suggests
     that command files are C programs.




































